# =============================================================================
# LandingOS workspace root — UNIVERSAL ignores only.
#
# Anything that applies to one product belongs in that product's own
# .gitignore (apps/<product>/.gitignore), never here. This is not tidiness:
# ignore patterns are matched relative to the file that declares them, so a
# root-level pattern silently reaches into every current and future product.
#
# The concrete case that forced this split: the website-builder's .gitignore
# carries a bare `test` pattern. Hoisted to the root it would untrack the
# ERP's entire test/ directory — 293 tests — with no error and no diff.
#
# Rule: if a pattern would be wrong for a product that does not exist yet,
# it does not go in this file.
# =============================================================================

# Dependencies — hoisted to the root by npm workspaces, plus any that
# resolve locally to a workspace.
node_modules/

# Environment / secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
